#
# THE FORWARD COVER WAS TAKEN UP ON 2026-08-29, AND IT WAS TOO NARROW.
# ST0010 rehydrated seven WP extracts plus info/design/acceptance, and the
# enumeration below covered info.md and acceptance.md and nothing else. The
# first attachment to land on disk, `intent/st/ST0010/design.md`, fell straight
# through: prettier realigned its tables, `prettier --check` now calls it clean,
# and the renderer's own output is NOT prettier-clean -- so the file no longer
# hashes to what the store records and doctor reports `attachment-drift`.
#
# THAT IS THE FAILURE THE PARAGRAPH ABOVE PREDICTED, one file over. The skew
# survives its own remedy: `sync --to-disk` rewrites design.md and the next
# commit that stages it reformats the repair back out, silently, forever.
#
# So the enumeration is replaced by the PRINCIPLE it was standing in for.
# Everything under `intent/st/` is written by the renderer from the canon
# store -- generated views and rendered attachments alike -- so all of it has
# one writer and none of it is the formatter's to touch. An enumeration has to
# be extended every time the store learns a new file name, and nothing reports
# the gap in between; a prefix cannot develop that gap.
#
# Renderer-owned paths only. intent/wip.md and intent/done.md are authored,
# stay formatted, and are deliberately absent.
#
# `**` not `*`: .prettierignore is gitignore syntax, where a single `*` will
# not cross a `/`.
